 "sanity_interpretation": "Interpretation: the catastrophic v1.0 identity-collapse signature is NOT reproduced by the selected EMA. In v1.0 (M7D1-N2 F01), every EMA candidate gave u8 x_hat == x_t, with A ~ 0 (budget pinned at the 0.01 hinge) and a vanishing background/landmark change. Here, 0 of 1905 VAL outputs are u8-identical to their target; on median only 4.2% of pixels are u8-identical. The mean |x_hat - x_t| is 0.016 (max 0.22). The artifact map A has mean 0.018 (median 0.016; the 5th percentile, 0.0082, lies below the 0.01 budget floor). The HF residual magnitude, 0.055, is comparable to the target's own HF magnitude, 0.062. Observation (non-gating, consistent with N5): the mask stays saturated open (mean M 0.9997; M > 0.5 on effectively every pixel), and ID cosine stays very high (0.9994), so the edit preserves identity while injecting HF artifact energy. No post-hoc threshold was applied, and the frozen-rule winner stands.",
